; RUN: %solver --array-equality -s %s 2>&1 | %OutputCheck %s
; CHECK-L: after eager equality instantiation:
; CHECK: ^unsat
; Three hundred constant access indexes alongside four symbolic ones. A
; comparison between two constant indexes is decided rather than built, so
; the constants cost only what they cost against the symbolic indexes and
; the arm is affordable here.
;
; Counted any other way it is not. A read count reports over three hundred
; and a pairwise count over forty-five thousand; the first of those is what
; the policy used to gate on, and it refused this query before anything
; could tell it that almost every pair was free.
;
; The disequality is between two store chains rather than between two array
; symbols, so it survives substitution and the procedure is still active
; when the policy runs -- see 76.
